Text: Provisional Constitution of the Federal Republic of Somalia, adopted 1 August 2012 (English version), as published on the website of the Federal Parliament of Somalia (https://parliament.gov.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Provisional-Constitution-2012.pdf). The site states no licence; the official legal text is reproduced for reference with attribution to the publisher.

The arrangement of this repository, its commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository is not legal advice and not an official publication.

Penal Code (Codice penale, Decreto legislativo 16 dicembre 1962, n. 5): Italian text recognised by OCR from a scan
of a printed edition of the code (the decree note gives its publication in the Bollettino Ufficiale, Supplemento n. 1 al n. 10 of 2 October 1963) held by Universita Roma Tre, Archivio Leggi
della Somalia (1950-1989), https://arcadia.sba.uniroma3.it/handle/2307/17142, retrieved 30 October 2026. Roma Tre is the
host of the bytes, not the publisher of the law. Laws are not protected by copyright in Somalia: Somali Democratic
Republic Copyright Law, Law No. 66 of 7 September 1977 (Official Bulletin No. 11 of 1 November 1977), Qoddobka 5aad
(Article 5), which lists among the works the author's right does not protect: "Sharciyada iyo xeerarka Hawladda"
(laws and government regulations). Source of the clause: the Somali text of Law No. 66 and its English outline of the
main provisions at https://www.somalilandlaw.com/somaliland_copyright_law.html (read 30 October 2026; whether Law
No. 66 is still applied in Somalia is not settled, and no later copyright act was found).
Changes made by Lexifina: OCR; removal of running heads, rule lines, footnote markers and headings; joining of wrapped
lines and hyphenated words; paragraph numbers normalised. The wording was not otherwise changed.
